Follow-up from k203 and k214 (2026-11-22). Two readers now decode UE text files the way FFileHelper::BufferToString does (UTF-16 LE/BE behind a BOM with an even length, otherwise UTF-8 with an optional BOM; UE 5.8.4 Runtime/Core/Private/Misc/FileHelper.cpp 145-185):
- decodeUEText in internal/config/engine.go (k203, the .uproject's EngineAssociation),
- the .uplugin/.uproject reader readUEJSON in cmd/launcher/uplugin.go (k214).
internal/config cannot import cmd/launcher, so the shared helper belongs in internal/config (or a small internal package) and uplugin.go calls it.

Keep the JSON handling apart: the engine reads EngineAssociation with TJsonReader, which refuses trailing commas (DesktopPlatformBase.cpp 1661-1678), while plugin and project descriptors go through RapidJSON with trailing commas allowed. Only the text decoding is shared.

Same card: parseLauncherInstalled (internal/config/engine.go, k211) still reads LauncherInstalled.dat as UTF-8 only, where the engine accepts UTF-16 too; with the shared decoder it is a one-word change. The unreagent-ue skill lists this gap in its Launcher installs row - update it with the fix.

Owner: unreagent-worker; skill-author for the unreagent-ue row. Done when one decoder serves all three readers, with its tests, and behaviour is unchanged otherwise.
